'If you have nothing to hide, you have nothing to fear' is historically illiterate — Stasi files show 600,000 East Germans were under surveillance for activities we would consider entirely lawful.
The right to develop ideas privately before sharing them — intellectual privacy — is foundational to creative work, scientific thinking, and political dissent.
Cambridge Analytica demonstrated that psychological profiles built from social data can be used to manipulate political behaviour at scale — a direct threat to democratic integrity.
